{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Is it not laid up with me, sealed.</b> Their wine is stored with me until they drink it. And how is it sealed? 'Vengeance and recompense are mine' — that is, the vengeance that I will exact from them is stored with me; this is the meaning of לי נקם ולי שלם — 'mine is vengeance and mine is recompense,' in the manner of what is said (Psalms 91:8): ״ושלומת רשעים תראה״. 'For the day of their calamity is at hand' — when their measure is full, in the manner of what is said (Genesis 15:16): ״כי לא שלם עון האמורי״." "<b>And it is possible</b> to interpret 'is it not laid up with me' as referring back to the word לאחריתם that he mentioned: he says that the end of the wicked who subjugate us is laid up with the Holy One, blessed be He, and sealed in His storehouses. And so we find in Daniel, who asked (Daniel 12:8): ״מה אחרית אלה״, and the Holy One, blessed be He, told him that these matters are hidden and sealed ״עד עת קץ״ — and that is the time when 'their foot shall slip.' 'For the day of their calamity is at hand' — at the time when they think it is far off, it draws near to them, and each of the things destined to come hastens to come upon them." "<b>And there is</b> in the word למו a sign and allusion to redemption, for then 'HaShem will judge His people,' and the Holy One, blessed be He, for the sake of His great Name, will hasten and speed it; and concerning that time He mentioned above (Deuteronomy 30:6): ״ומל ה' אלהיך את לבבך״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:28.931717509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}